# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): `REQ-ASK` in a joint model, "a member's ask named as asked, a.q (L §6.1)". The
# joint model of L6_1_member_path: its own ask r and its member a, which declares no ask (a.rate is an item). The
# request names r, then a.zz, which a doesn't declare: the run prints the one refusal and r isn't answered.
# Was `refused: LOAD-NAME no ask a.zz`, after r had been answered.
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "members/ana.tally" sha256 "caf5f7622e7fa75fe10974cb18199597c91e70a92e887654d54870c36f543c67"

ask r: a.rate
=== members/ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== expect r a.zz
refused: REQ-ASK no ask a.zz
